# Optional NON-SECRET overrides. Copy to .env before the first setup only.
# Never put a PAT, GH_TOKEN, registration token, or removal token here.
RUNNER_REPOSITORY=es94111/Health_Passbook_Dashboard
RUNNER_NAME=health-passbook-dependabot-linux-x64

# Prerequisites: Docker Desktop (Compose + amd64 emulation), gh auth login, jq.
# Setup: ./manage.sh setup    Status: ./manage.sh status
# Verify: ./manage.sh verify  Pause: ./manage.sh stop
# Resume: ./manage.sh start   Re-register: ./manage.sh reregister
# Unregister: ./manage.sh unregister (retains all named volumes).
# Docker Desktop must be running; enable its login startup for Mac reboot recovery.
# Restart policy is unless-stopped: explicit stops remain stopped after reboot.
# Both services share /home/runner/_work, not the Mac's Docker socket or folders.
# The dedicated DinD daemon is privileged inside Docker Desktop's Linux VM.
# Do not expose it to untrusted jobs; this is not a VM-grade security boundary.
# Keep general CI jobs pinned to [self-hosted, macOS, X64].
# Dependabot requires a private repository and Settings > Code security >
# Dependabot > Runner type: Labeled runner (dependabot), or the older
# "Dependabot on self-hosted runners" setting enabled. Setup does not change it.
# Do not run compose down --volumes: runner-state contains registration credentials.
